&lt;h3&gt;


  Clean Modular Architecture (Zero Heavyweight Framework Overhead):
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Week 3/
├── index.html                 # Semantic HTML5, Tailwind v4 theme, modal drawers &amp;amp; accessible UI
├── style.css                  # Custom tokens, tactile shadows, cross-browser scrollbars
├── favicon.svg                # Scalable vector sloth chef mascot with dark-mode awareness
├── package.json               # Lightweight development server scripts
├── .gitignore                 # Secrets, OS junk, logs, and build artifacts exclusion
├── .vscode/settings.json      # Workspace CSS &amp;amp; HTML linting configuration
└── js/
    ├── config.js              # Storage keys, pantry staples, cooking modes, pure veg regex rules
    ├── audio.js               # Web Audio API sound synthesizer (warm pentatonic pop &amp;amp; chime notes)
    ├── state.js               # Reactive state container, localStorage sync &amp;amp; canonical deduplication
    ├── timer.js               # Sloth Nap hands-free timer with Web Speech API voice synthesis
    ├── substitutions.js       # Pure veg zero-store pantry substitutions engine &amp;amp; AI rephraser
    ├── recipes-data.js        # Curated offline pure veg culinary database
    ├── recipe-engine.js       # Recipe synthesis engine &amp;amp; single-vessel constraint enforcer
    ├── gemini.js              # Google AI Studio dynamic model probe &amp;amp; API caller
    ├── scanner.js             # Client-side FileReader fridge photo dropzone &amp;amp; local visual analyzer
    ├── ui.js                  # DOM visual bindings, theme toggle, toasts &amp;amp; modals
    └── app.js                 # Application bootstrap &amp;amp; lifecycle orchestration
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


  How I Built It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fridge-to-Feast is built around a resilient &lt;strong&gt;hybrid AI and local-first architecture&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Vision &amp;amp; Recipe Synthesis (Google AI Studio / Gemini API)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses &lt;code&gt;gemini-1.5-flash&lt;/code&gt; with dynamic fallback across Gemini models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspects raw fridge photos to identify edible vegetarian produce and builds customized step-by-step recipes tailored to the user's chosen energy level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When substituting ingredients, a dedicated AI rephrasing prompt rewrites instructions so cooking steps accurately reflect the culinary nature of the replacement item.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Offline Sloth Engine (Resilient Local Heuristic Inference)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When offline or when no API key is provided, the app seamlessly engages a &lt;strong&gt;local-first heuristic recipe engine&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backed by &lt;code&gt;OFFLINE_RECIPES_DATABASE&lt;/code&gt; and procedural single-vessel synthesis with canonical stem deduplication (using &lt;code&gt;getCanonicalStem&lt;/code&gt;), ensuring ingredients and steps are never awkwardly repeated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pure Vegetarian Guardrails&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A multi-tier regex and keyword sanitizer actively screens inputs to ensure 100% vegetarian compliance, preventing accidental non-veg contamination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Web Audio &amp;amp; Web Speech APIs&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instead of loading heavy external MP3 audio assets, tactile clicks and soothing chimes are generated entirely in real-time via the browser's &lt;code&gt;AudioContext&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Sloth Nap Timer discovers system neural voices (such as Microsoft Aria/Jenny or macOS Samantha) to deliver unhurried, gentle wake-up announcements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Why Does Open Innovation Matter?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kitchen Privacy &amp;amp; Personal Sovereignty&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
Your personal fridge photos, dietary habits, and grocery inventory stay where they belong: inside your browser's &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;. Closed commercial apps monetize user grocery data; open innovation guarantees user privacy by default.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resilience Across the Offline Gap&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
Cooking happens in real-world kitchens where Wi-Fi drops or data signals lag. By pairing open-source AI with local algorithmic heuristic engines, users can cook hot meals even when completely disconnected from the internet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zero Paywalls for Daily Sustenance&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
Nobody should have to pay a recurring monthly subscription or hit API rate limits just to figure out what to cook with leftover potatoes and rice. Open-source keeps technology accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community-Tailored Culinary Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
Proprietary cooking apps frequently overlook global vegetarian traditions. An open-source codebase empowers developers worldwide to contribute regional pantry staples, spices, and authentic vegetarian substitution cheat sheets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




