&lt;h2&gt;


  Quando serve un'API REST
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un'&lt;strong&gt;API REST&lt;/strong&gt; diventa necessaria quando il backend deve servire più client: un'app mobile, un frontend separato (SPA React, Vue, Angular), un gestionale di terze parti o un'integrazione con servizi esterni. Invece di duplicare la logica di business in ogni client, un'API centralizza dati e regole in un &lt;strong&gt;unico punto di accesso&lt;/strong&gt;, garantendo coerenza e riducendo drasticamente la manutenzione.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;strong&gt;PHP moderno&lt;/strong&gt;, costruire un'API REST è un'operazione naturale: controller dedicati con single responsibility, middleware per autenticazione e rate limiting, risposte JSON strutturate con codici HTTP semantici, e validazione degli input con regole chiare e messaggi di errore utili.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Scenari concreti in cui un'API è la scelta giusta
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;App mobile + web&lt;/strong&gt;: la stessa logica di business serve sia il sito web che l'app iOS/Android. L'API è il punto comune&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend SPA&lt;/strong&gt;: un frontend React o Vue che comunica con il backend via JSON, per un'esperienza utente più fluida e reattiva&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Integrazioni B2B&lt;/strong&gt;: partner commerciali, fornitori o clienti che devono accedere a dati o funzionalità in modo automatizzato&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Microservizi&lt;/strong&gt;: un'architettura dove servizi indipendenti comunicano tra loro via HTTP/REST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Automazioni interne&lt;/strong&gt;: script, cron job, webhook e processi automatizzati che interagiscono con il sistema principale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Come si struttura un'API REST in PHP
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La progettazione di un'API REST solida parte da principi architetturali chiari. Non basta restituire JSON da un controller — serve una &lt;strong&gt;struttura coerente e prevedibile&lt;/strong&gt; che i client possano consumare con fiducia.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Endpoint RESTful: la convenzione che semplifica tutto
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I verbi HTTP hanno un significato preciso in REST:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GET /api/articles&lt;/strong&gt;: lista delle risorse (con paginazione, filtri, ordinamento)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GET /api/articles/{id}&lt;/strong&gt;: dettaglio di una singola risorsa&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;POST /api/articles&lt;/strong&gt;: creazione di una nuova risorsa&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;PUT /api/articles/{id}&lt;/strong&gt;: aggiornamento completo di una risorsa esistente&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;PATCH /api/articles/{id}&lt;/strong&gt;: aggiornamento parziale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;DELETE /api/articles/{id}&lt;/strong&gt;: eliminazione di una risorsa&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Questa convenzione rende l'API &lt;strong&gt;auto-documentante&lt;/strong&gt;: un client che conosce REST sa già come interagire con le risorse senza leggere pagine di documentazione.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Autenticazione e sicurezza
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un'API pubblica senza autenticazione è un invito agli abusi. Le strategie più comuni in PHP:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;JWT (JSON Web Token)&lt;/strong&gt;: token stateless che il client invia nell'header Authorization. Ideale per SPA e app mobile, perché non richiede sessioni server-side&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;API Key&lt;/strong&gt;: chiave univoca per identificare il client. Semplice da implementare, adatta per integrazioni server-to-server&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;OAuth 2.0&lt;/strong&gt;: per scenari più complessi con delegazione di accesso (es. "Login con Google")&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Oltre all'autenticazione, una buona API implementa: &lt;strong&gt;rate limiting&lt;/strong&gt; per prevenire abusi, CORS configurato correttamente per i client browser, HTTPS obbligatorio, e input sanitization per prevenire injection.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Validazione input: la prima linea di difesa
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ogni dato in ingresso va validato prima di raggiungere la logica di business. In PHP moderno, la validazione si implementa con regole dichiarative:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tipi di dato (string, int, email, URL, date)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vincoli (required, max length, min value, regex pattern)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relazioni (exists in database, unique, confirmed)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Le risposte di errore seguono un formato standard con &lt;strong&gt;codice HTTP 422&lt;/strong&gt; (Unprocessable Entity) e un body JSON che elenca i campi invalidi con messaggi leggibili.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Risposte JSON strutturate
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Una buona API restituisce risposte coerenti con &lt;strong&gt;codici di stato HTTP appropriati&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;200 OK&lt;/strong&gt;: richiesta elaborata con successo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;201 Created&lt;/strong&gt;: risorsa creata con successo (POST)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;204 No Content&lt;/strong&gt;: operazione riuscita senza body (DELETE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;400 Bad Request&lt;/strong&gt;: richiesta malformata&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;401 Unauthorized&lt;/strong&gt;: autenticazione mancante o invalida&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;403 Forbidden&lt;/strong&gt;: autenticato ma non autorizzato&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;404 Not Found&lt;/strong&gt;: risorsa non trovata&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;429 Too Many Requests&lt;/strong&gt;: rate limit superato&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;500 Internal Server Error&lt;/strong&gt;: errore server non gestito&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Versioning: pianificare l'evoluzione
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un'API evolve nel tempo, e i client esistenti non devono rompersi quando si introducono cambiamenti. Il &lt;strong&gt;versioning&lt;/strong&gt; è essenziale:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;URL versioning&lt;/strong&gt;: /api/v1/articles — semplice e visibile, la scelta più pragmatica&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Header versioning&lt;/strong&gt;: Accept: application/vnd.api+json;version=1 — più "puro" ma meno immediato&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La regola d'oro: le breaking change vanno in una nuova versione. Le aggiunte retrocompatibili (nuovi campi, nuovi endpoint) si possono rilasciare nella versione corrente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Documentazione: OpenAPI e Swagger
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un'API senza documentazione è un'API che nessuno userà correttamente. Lo standard &lt;strong&gt;OpenAPI (Swagger)&lt;/strong&gt; permette di descrivere endpoint, parametri, risposte ed errori in formato machine-readable (YAML/JSON). Da questa specifica si generano automaticamente: documentazione interattiva, client SDK in qualsiasi linguaggio, test di conformità.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In PHP, librerie come &lt;strong&gt;L5-Swagger&lt;/strong&gt; o &lt;strong&gt;Scribe&lt;/strong&gt; generano la specifica OpenAPI direttamente dal codice e dalle annotation, mantenendo documentazione e implementazione sempre sincronizzate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Vantaggi concreti di un'API REST ben progettata
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un'API ben progettata separa frontend e backend, rende il sistema testabile in isolamento e apre la porta a integrazioni future senza modificare il core. È un &lt;strong&gt;investimento architetturale&lt;/strong&gt; che paga nel medio e lungo termine:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Riusabilità&lt;/strong&gt;: la stessa API serve web, mobile, integrazioni e automazioni&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Testabilità&lt;/strong&gt;: ogni endpoint si testa indipendentemente con test automatizzati&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Scalabilità&lt;/strong&gt;: frontend e backend scalano indipendentemente&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Manutenibilità&lt;/strong&gt;: logica centralizzata, modifiche in un solo punto&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Time to market&lt;/strong&gt;: nuovi client (app mobile, partner) si collegano senza modificare il backend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se il tuo progetto prevede più di un'interfaccia utente, integrazioni con terze parti o potrebbe evolversi in quella direzione, progettare un'&lt;strong&gt;API REST fin dall'inizio&lt;/strong&gt; è la decisione architetturale più lungimirante che puoi prendere.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;👉 &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://iadicola.it/articoli/sviluppo-api-rest-in-php-quando-serve-e-come-si-struttura?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=social" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Leggi l'articolo completo su iadicola.it&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Free-Work is the main French job board for IT: about 10,000 live postings, half of them freelance missions with a daily rate (TJM). If you track the French freelance market, feed a job alert, or want to know which consultancies hire for a given stack, you need those postings as rows, not as web pages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is how to get them as clean JSON or CSV in a few minutes, with an Apify Actor I maintain. No login, no proxy, no code required, and it respects the site's robots.txt.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Run it once
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open the Actor page: &lt;a href="https://apify.com/bibian/free-work-jobs-scraper" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Free-Work Jobs &amp;amp; Freelance Missions Scraper&lt;/a&gt; and click &lt;strong&gt;Try for free&lt;/strong&gt;. The form is already filled with a working example: keywords &lt;code&gt;data engineer&lt;/code&gt;, postings of the last 7 days, 50 results. Click &lt;strong&gt;Start&lt;/strong&gt;. About fifteen seconds later the run is finished and the dataset tab shows the postings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each record looks like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"title"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Data Engineer"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"companyName"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"STHREE SAS"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"contracts"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"contractor"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"experienceLevel"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"senior"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"remoteMode"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"partial"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"locationLabel"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Paris, France"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"minDailyRate"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;550&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"maxDailyRate"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;650&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"currency"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"EUR"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"durationValue"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"durationPeriod"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"month"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"skills"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"AWS Cloud"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Databricks"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"PySpark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Python"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"SQL"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"publishedAt"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2026-10-01T11:18:03+02:00"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"url"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https://www.free-work.com/fr/tech-it/job-mission/data-engineer/data-engineer-1419"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Permanent jobs carry &lt;code&gt;minAnnualSalary&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;maxAnnualSalary&lt;/code&gt; instead of the daily rates. Export the dataset as JSON, CSV or Excel from the same page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. Make it a daily alert
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Save the run as a &lt;strong&gt;Task&lt;/strong&gt; and set &lt;strong&gt;Published within (days)&lt;/strong&gt; to &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add a &lt;strong&gt;Schedule&lt;/strong&gt; to the task: every weekday at 7:00.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add an &lt;strong&gt;Integration&lt;/strong&gt; to the task: Google Sheets (append rows), Slack, or a webhook to your own endpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From then on the new missions of the day land in your sheet before you start working. Deduplicate on the &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; field if you keep your own copy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. Or call it from your code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;JavaScript:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;apify-client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;APIFY_TOKEN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;actor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bibian/free-work-jobs-scraper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;keywords&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;python&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;publishedWithinDays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;maxItems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dataset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;defaultDatasetId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;listItems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Python:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;apify_client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;lt;APIFY_TOKEN&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;actor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;bibian/free-work-jobs-scraper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run_input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;keywords&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;python&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;publishedWithinDays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;maxItems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dataset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;defaultDatasetId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;list_items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Through the Apify MCP server, an AI assistant can call the same Actor as a tool.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What it costs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pay per result: $2.00 per 1,000 postings, plus $0.01 per run. The example above, 50 postings, costs about $0.11. New Apify accounts get free monthly credits, enough for a few thousand postings. There is no subscription.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What it does not do
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It reads the public listing and posting pages only. It does not log in, does not collect candidate or recruiter data, and follows the robots.txt rules of free-work.com. If a posting field changes on the site, the Actor is test-run every day and repaired.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Questions or a missing field? Open an issue on the &lt;a href="https://apify.com/bibian/free-work-jobs-scraper" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Actor page&lt;/a&gt;, I read them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not a hype list. These are the three MCP servers I have running right now in Claude Desktop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Filesystem
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mcp-hub &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I use this to let Claude read project files directly instead of me copy-pasting code. Configure it to point at your project root.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real usage&lt;/strong&gt;: "Read the auth module and explain how the token validation works."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. GitHub
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mcp-hub &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; @modelcontextprotocol/server-github
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Lets Claude check issues, read PRs, and browse repos. I use it for code reviews.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real usage&lt;/strong&gt;: "Check what changed in the last 3 PRs and summarize."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. PostgreSQL
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mcp-hub &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; @modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Direct database access from Claude. I run queries without leaving the conversation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real usage&lt;/strong&gt;: "Show me users who signed up this week but haven't logged in."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Setup
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each one takes 2 minutes:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;mcp-hub &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install&lt;/span&gt; &amp;lt;server&amp;gt;
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Add to claude_desktop_config.json&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Restart Claude Desktop&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  Warning
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The filesystem server can read your entire disk if you configure it that way. Be careful with paths.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;All servers verified on npm. &lt;a href="https://github.com/GrahamduesCN/mcp-platform" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;mcp-hub&lt;/a&gt; CLI to discover more.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You have a good photo and an idea for a short video. What you probably do not have is a shot list, a folder of matching clips, or the patience to write a different prompt for every cut.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A template can handle that planning. You choose the scene, supply the subject, review the cost, and let the workflow build the shots and join them into a vertical film.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Disclosure: I build ModelFold, the product used in this walkthrough. This is a guide to its current workflow, not a comparison based on testing competing tools. The examples are existing template previews; I did not run a new paid generation for this article.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Start with the result you want
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open the &lt;a href="https://ai.modelfold.online/tools/ai-short-video" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;AI Short Video tool&lt;/a&gt; and look through the template previews. A preview shows the intended scene and style. It is not a prediction of exactly how your photo will turn out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a simple first project, try one of these:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://ai.modelfold.online/short-video/templates/pet-rainbow-bridge" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pet marigold bridge&lt;/a&gt;: a quiet, 10-second memorial with two shots, warm mist, petals, and candlelight. The name references the rainbow bridge idea, but the actual scene uses a marigold-covered bridge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://ai.modelfold.online/short-video/templates/ai-pet-chef" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pet chef&lt;/a&gt;: a playful kitchen scene built around a pet photo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choose a scene that suits the photo you already have. A pet template needs a clear pet reference; a portrait effect needs a face the model can actually see.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Prepare one clear reference image
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use a JPG, PNG, or WebP file up to 3MB. Prefer one obvious subject, good lighting, and minimal obstruction. If you want the model to preserve a pet's markings, make sure those markings are visible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Leave a little space around the subject. A tight landscape crop can be awkward to reinterpret as a 9:16 frame. Only upload photos you have permission to use, especially when they show another person.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same uploaded image serves as the reference for the template's shots. You do not need a separate upload for each scene. That shared reference helps guide consistency, but AI can still change facial features, fur patterns, or proportions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. Read the shot list before generating
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open a template and sign in. Upload the image, then read the shots and model settings on the page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the memorial template, the first shot has the pet walking toward the camera across the bridge. The second has it pause and look back. Together they make a 10-second vertical video. The configured workflow creates the still frames with Seedream 5.0 Flash and animates them with Wan 2.6 Flash at 720p.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Templates have fixed creative choices. This one does not add a spoken tribute or captions. If you want a name and dates, add them to the downloaded video in an editor.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Read product templates especially carefully. A scene that asks for an unbranded object and no text is a poor choice if your packaging label must stay legible. A visually attractive preview does not establish that a template can preserve a logo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. Check the estimate and confirm
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Opening the page, watching a preview, and selecting a template do not spend generation credits. Generating your video does.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Check the estimated credits on the page and again in the confirmation dialog. Prices depend on the configured image and video steps, so use the current estimate rather than a number copied from an old tutorial.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fixed template already includes its shot plan; you do not first pay to generate alternative plans. Each generation step is charged separately. Failed steps are refunded, while successful steps remain charged. Retrying a step is a new generation and can incur another charge.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4. Let the workflow assemble the film
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The progress panel lists the still images, video clips, and final joining step. You do not have to download each shot and stitch them together yourself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once a result is ready, the player switches from the example to your film. Review the subject carefully before using it: does your pet still look like your pet? Are movement and proportions plausible? Does the scene communicate what you intended?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If only part of a run succeeds, the finished portion may be available and the failed steps refunded. Check the status rather than assuming that a playable result means every shot succeeded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Download, then finish it for your audience
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Download the MP4. Signed-in history on the tool page also lets you revisit the run, its steps, and its download.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a memorial, a simple title may be enough. For a social post, you may want captions or a short opening line. Add those deliberately in your editor rather than relying on generated text inside the image.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ModelFold does not automatically post the file to another platform. Download it, review it, and upload it yourself. Follow the destination platform's rules for disclosing AI-generated content.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What if no template fits?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same tool has a free-form route. Describe the film, set the duration and shot count if needed, and request plans. For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A 15-second vertical video with three shots of a white travel mug: a full view, a close-up of the lid, then the mug on a commuter's desk. Natural light and restrained camera movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Review the proposed plans, models, and estimates before executing one. Planning uses a conversation model and has its own charge; generating the images and clips is a separate stage. It gives you more flexibility, with more decisions to make.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a first attempt, a fixed template keeps those decisions manageable: choose the scene, upload a suitable photo, read the estimate, generate, and inspect the download.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can browse the examples at &lt;a href="https://ai.modelfold.online/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;ModelFold&lt;/a&gt; before deciding whether the workflow fits your project.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  Adding a Public‑Facing Agenda, Private Chat, and Commission‑Based Payments to a Next.js Marketplace
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I extended the public section of the Home Services Marketplace with agenda visibility, a private messaging UI, and a commission‑aware payment flow. The changes required new Prisma models, a migration script, env tweaks, and a handful of page component updates in the Next.js 14 app router.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The MVP only let users browse providers; there was no way to see a provider’s available slots, exchange messages, or pay through the platform. The UI showed a static home page and a generic FAQ, while the back‑end lacked any data structures for appointments, chat threads, or payment records. The missing pieces manifested as:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;404 / “Agenda not found”&lt;/strong&gt; when trying to hit &lt;code&gt;/profesionales/[slug]/agenda&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;TypeScript errors&lt;/strong&gt; because &lt;code&gt;Appointment&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Message&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;Payment&lt;/code&gt; types were undefined in the Prisma schema.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Runtime crash&lt;/strong&gt; in the FAQ page when &lt;code&gt;getSettings()&lt;/code&gt; was called without being imported.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No environment variable&lt;/strong&gt; for a payment provider, causing the payment service to fallback to a disabled stub.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These blockers prevented us from delivering the core “book‑and‑pay” loop that a marketplace needs.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was to patch the UI only, adding placeholder components that displayed hard‑coded appointment slots and a dummy chat box. I added a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; hook in &lt;code&gt;src/app/(publico)/profesionales/[slug]/page.tsx&lt;/code&gt; that fetched a static JSON file with schedule data. The approach failed for two reasons:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Data inconsistency&lt;/strong&gt; – The hard‑coded schedule quickly diverged from the actual provider availability stored in the database.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No persistence&lt;/strong&gt; – Messages and payments never reached the back‑end, so the system could not enforce commissions or keep a traceable record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I also tried to enable payments by setting &lt;code&gt;PAYMENTS_PROVIDER=disabled&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;.env.example&lt;/code&gt;, but the payment service threw &lt;code&gt;Error: Payments are disabled in the current environment&lt;/code&gt;, which halted the checkout flow entirely.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Database – New Models &amp;amp; Migration
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I introduced three new Prisma models: &lt;code&gt;Appointment&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Message&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;Payment&lt;/code&gt;. The migration lives in &lt;code&gt;prisma/migrations/20261024000000_agenda_chat_pagos_expediente_legal/migration.sql&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight sql"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;-- migration.sql (excerpt)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;CREATE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;TABLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"Appointment"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;SERIAL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;PRIMARY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"providerId"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;INTEGER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"User"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"clientId"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;INTEGER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"User"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"startAt"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TIMESTAMP&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"endAt"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TIMESTAMP&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TEXT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;DEFAULT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'pending'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;CREATE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;TABLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"Message"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;SERIAL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;PRIMARY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"conversationId"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;INTEGER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"senderId"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;INTEGER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"User"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"content"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TEXT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"sentAt"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TIMESTAMP&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;DEFAULT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;CREATE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;TABLE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"Payment"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;SERIAL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;PRIMARY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"appointmentId"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;INTEGER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"Appointment"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;"id"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"amountCents"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;INTEGER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"commissionCents"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;INTEGER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nv"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TEXT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NOT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;NULL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;DEFAULT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'awaiting'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Corresponding updates in &lt;code&gt;prisma/schema.prisma&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;model Appointment {
  id          Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
  provider    User     @relation(fields: [providerId], references: [id])
  providerId  Int
  client      User     @relation(fields: [clientId], references: [id])
  clientId    Int
  startAt     DateTime
  endAt       DateTime
  status      String   @default("pending")
  payment     Payment?
}

model Message {
  id             Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
  conversationId Int
  sender         User     @relation(fields: [senderId], references: [id])
  senderId       Int
  content        String
  sentAt         DateTime @default(now())
}

model Payment {
  id               Int        @id @default(autoincrement())
  appointment      Appointment @relation(fields: [appointmentId], references: [id])
  appointmentId    Int
  amountCents      Int
  commissionCents  Int
  status           String     @default("awaiting")
}
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Running &lt;code&gt;npx prisma migrate dev&lt;/code&gt; applied the schema and generated the new tables.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Environment – Enabling Payments
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I replaced the placeholder in &lt;code&gt;.env.example&lt;/code&gt; with a real provider flag and added a comment explaining the toggle.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# Payments: set to "stripe" for production, "test" for sandbox, or "disabled" for MVP
PAYMENTS_PROVIDER=test
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;.gitignore&lt;/code&gt; was also updated to avoid committing legal source imports:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# ...
+.legal-sources/
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Public Pages – Hooking UI to the New Data
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


  Home (&lt;code&gt;src/app/(publico)/page.tsx&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I added icons for the new agenda and chat features and wired the CTA to the provider microsite.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ArrowRight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;BadgeCheck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CalendarDays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;FileCheck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Lock&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MapPin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;lucide-react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PublicHome&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"grid gap-6"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* Existing hero */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/agenda"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex items-center"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CalendarDays&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"mr-2"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; View Provider Agenda
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/chat"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex items-center"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Lock&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"mr-2"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; Private Messaging
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h4&gt;


  FAQ (&lt;code&gt;src/app/(publico)/preguntas-frecuentes/page.tsx&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The page now pulls dynamic settings (e.g., commission rate) via the newly exported &lt;code&gt;getSettings&lt;/code&gt; service.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Metadata&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Link&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next/link&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;getSettings&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/modules/settings/service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PageHeader&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/ui/primitiv&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Metadata&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;FAQ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;FAQPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;settings&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getSettings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// &amp;lt;-- new import&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PageHeader&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Preguntas Frecuentes"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Commission: &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;settings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;commissionRate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;%&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* rest of FAQ */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



